{
  "hadith_number": 8,
  "text": "On the authority of the Son of Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the messenger of Allah made a blessings and peace of Allah be upon him, said, I have been ordered to fight against people, until they testify that there is no God but Allah, and that Muhammad is the messenger of Allah, and until they perform the prayers and pay the zakat, and if they do so, they will have gained protection from me for their lives and property, unless they do acts that are punishable in accordance with Islam, and their reckoning will be with Allah the Almighty. It was related by Al-Bukhari and Muslim.",
